Callable after find_tools:
- search_worker — Find a driver or other worker by name or code, or list the roster.
- list_carriers — List the carriers this organization tenders freight to, narrowed by status, compliance, safety rating or authority number.
- shipment_list — Find shipments (loads) by the words people use for them, by status, or by filters on dates, charges and transfer status.
- settlement_list_pay_events — List driver pay events, the pay a driver earned per load, newest first.
- get_worker_earnings_summary — Summarize what a worker has earned but not yet been paid on a settlement.
- settlement_start_dispute_review — Move an open pay dispute a driver raised to under review, so the driver and the team see someone is looking into it.
- settlement_generate_driver_batch — Generate the pay period's driver settlement batch: a draft settlement for every driver with accrued, unheld pay who has none for the period yet.
- settlement_attach_pay_events — Add a driver's accrued pay events to their draft driver settlement, such as a late load that missed generation.
- settlement_detach_pay_event — Take one load's pay off a draft driver settlement and return it to the unsettled pool, such as pay that belongs to the next period or is disputed.
- settlement_hold_pay_event — Hold a driver's accrued pay for one load so it skips settlement until released, with the reason.
- settlement_release_pay_event — Release a held driver pay event back into the pool the next settlement draws from.
- settlement_remove_driver_adjustment — Remove a manual adjustment line from a draft or pending driver settlement.
- settlement_submit_driver — Submit a draft driver settlement for approval once its lines are right.
- settlement_approve_driver — Propose approving pending driver settlements, one or up to 50 in one proposal the person decides together.
- settlement_reject_driver — Send a driver settlement that is pending approval back to draft, with the reason.
- settlement_post_driver — Propose posting approved driver settlements to the general ledger, one or up to 50 in one proposal the person decides together.
- settlement_record_driver_payment — Propose recording that a posted driver settlement was paid, with how and the reference.
- settlement_void_driver — Propose voiding a driver settlement that is not yet paid, with the reason.
- settlement_pay_now — Propose paying a driver now, off cycle, for pay they have accrued.
- settlement_generate_carrier_batch — Generate the pay period's carrier settlement batch, a draft settlement for each carrier with pending cost.
- settlement_remove_carrier_adjustment — Remove a manual adjustment line from a draft or pending carrier settlement.
- settlement_submit_carrier — Submit a draft carrier settlement for approval once its lines are right.
- settlement_approve_carrier — Propose approving pending carrier settlements, one or up to 50 in one proposal the person decides together.
- settlement_reject_carrier — Send a carrier settlement that is pending approval back to draft, with the reason.
- settlement_post_carrier — Propose posting approved carrier settlements to the general ledger, one or up to 50 in one proposal the person decides together.
- settlement_void_carrier — Propose voiding a carrier settlement that is not yet paid, with the reason.
- list_carrier_invoice_matches — List carrier freight invoices matched against what each load was expected to cost, with the variance.
- list_edi_carrier_invoices — List freight invoices carriers sent over EDI, newest first, with how each reconciles: Unmatched, MappingRequired when no carrier is linked, Matched or Variance.
- create_carrier_invoice_match — Match a carrier's EDI invoice to the load it bills, comparing its total with what the carrier assignment was expected to cost.
- accept_carrier_invoice_match — Propose accepting a carrier's invoice that matches what the load was expected to cost, clearing it for payment on the carrier's settlement.
- accept_carrier_invoice_match_with_variance — Propose accepting a carrier's invoice that differs from the expected cost and paying the difference.
- reject_carrier_invoice_match — Reject a carrier's invoice match that is wrong, such as an invoice for another load or a duplicate, with a note saying why.
- link_edi_carrier_invoice_to_carrier — Link an inbound EDI carrier invoice to the carrier in Trenova it came from, when its SCAC or DOT number did not find one, so it can be matched.
- settlement_list_advances — List driver pay advances, the cash and money codes given against future pay, newest first.
- settlement_issue_advance — Propose recording a cash or money-code advance a driver was given against future pay.
- settlement_forgive_advance — Propose writing off what is still owed on a driver's pay advance, so no more is recovered from their pay, with the reason.
- settlement_list_escrow_accounts — List owner-operator escrow accounts with the driver, status and when each opened or closed.
- settlement_adjust_escrow_account — Propose a manual adjustment to an owner-operator's escrow balance, with what it is for.
- settlement_list_pay_profiles — List the organization's driver pay profiles, the packages that say how a driver is paid per mile, per load or by percentage.
- settlement_list_pay_assignments — List a driver's pay profile assignments, newest first: which profile paid them from when to when, their share of each load, and which one is in force today.
- settlement_list_recurring_deductions — List drivers' recurring deductions, such as insurance, equipment lease or escrow contributions.
- settlement_list_recurring_earnings — List drivers' recurring earnings, such as per diem, a guaranteed stipend or a bonus paid over time.

What a change you call does:
- Changes that always record a proposal for a person to decide: raise_exception, flag_for_manual_review, wait_until, cancel_wait, settlement_start_dispute_review, settlement_resolve_dispute, settlement_generate_driver, settlement_generate_driver_batch, settlement_attach_pay_events, settlement_detach_pay_event, settlement_hold_pay_event, settlement_release_pay_event, settlement_add_driver_adjustment, settlement_remove_driver_adjustment, settlement_recalculate_driver, settlement_submit_driver, settlement_approve_driver, settlement_reject_driver, settlement_post_driver, settlement_record_driver_payment, settlement_void_driver, settlement_pay_now, settlement_generate_carrier_batch, settlement_add_carrier_adjustment, settlement_remove_carrier_adjustment, settlement_recalculate_carrier, settlement_submit_carrier, settlement_approve_carrier, settlement_reject_carrier, settlement_post_carrier, settlement_record_carrier_payment, settlement_void_carrier, create_carrier_invoice_match, accept_carrier_invoice_match, accept_carrier_invoice_match_with_variance, reject_carrier_invoice_match, link_edi_carrier_invoice_to_carrier, settlement_issue_advance, settlement_forgive_advance, settlement_adjust_escrow_account
